# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Daemon runtime logs (stray, shouldn't be tracked)
daemon/output.log
daemon/output2.log

# Runtime-generated, lives in ~/.cache/nisfere in a real install —
# only relevant here if you're testing against a repo-local cache path.
*.log

# packaging/<pkgname>/ folders should only ever track PKGBUILD.
# Everything else in there (src/, pkg/, built .pkg.tar.* files, .SRCINFO,
# makepkg logs, or a full nested git checkout if you ever clone one
# there directly) is build-time output or scratch space, recreated
# fresh by makepkg every run — never something to commit.
#
# The /* (not a bare trailing /) is deliberate: it matches CONTENTS of
# each packaging/<name>/ folder individually, rather than the folder
# itself as one ignored entry. If the folder itself were ignored as a
# single unit, git would never look inside it again at all, and the
# negation rule below couldn't "un-ignore" one specific file inside —
# matching per-file like this is what makes the exception work.
packaging/*/*
!packaging/*/PKGBUILD
